# Only the prebuilt output-py + requirements are needed to build the image.
#
# The stanza below looks redundant and is not. Docker will not re-include a
# path whose PARENT is excluded, so `*` followed by `!columns/python/output-py`
# ships nothing and the COPY fails with "not found". Each level has to be
# re-included and then re-narrowed on the way down.
#
# Keep it this shape. The obvious simplification does not build. (The previous
# version said `!output-py`, from before the 2026-07-30 restructure moved the
# artefact under columns/python/ — so this Dockerfile had never built at all.)
*
!requirements.txt

!columns
columns/*
!columns/python
columns/python/*
!columns/python/output-py
